      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a predictive model for a new property insurance product. We're trying to refine our neighborhood risk profiles to get better granularity on claim frequency. Financial data is all set, but the model is still showing a lot of unexplained variance. What kind of non-financial, demographic, or community-level variables would you suggest we look into to help tighten up the predictive accuracy for localized risk?",
